  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting a safe environment for children in Lomas de Carabayllo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Warmi Huasi is providing support to families in the shanty town of San Benito, Lomas de Carabayllo, on the northern outskirts of Peru&apos;s capital Lima. They are working to ensure that children who are left home alone for long periods whilst their parents go out to work are as protected as possible from potential risks to their safety, health and personal development. 
 
Warmi Huasi is working with children, mothers, community organisations and state institutions to develop an integral and sustainable system to protect children who are left home alone. In the period 2014-2016 they aim to document their research and methodology to share with other community and municipal institutions with the aim of multiplying the results further.</narrative>
  </description>
